Derive the following Circular Polarisation in a Linear Basis relation from the preceding result, showing the algebra, calculus, counting, or physical identity used at each step.
\[
\vec E_L(0,t)=\frac{E_0}{\sqrt2}
\operatorname{Re}\!\left\{(\hat e_1+i\hat e_2)e^{-i\omega t}\right\}
=\frac{E_0}{\sqrt2}(\hat e_1\cos\omega t+\hat e_2\sin\omega t).
\tag*{[2]}
\]
